":54.0,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.030276153952087718,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":43.4,"_gate_pool_share":-0.0465092817093663,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":21.4,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.02605624413386228,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":23.9,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.06482477604972114,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":83.1,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.057774976921304955,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":100.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0010585667515460168,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":98.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.0144299995,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":9.6,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"The Cigna Group, together with its subsidiaries, provides insurance and related products and services in the United States. It operates through two segments: Evernorth Health Services and Cigna Healthcare. The Evernorth Health Services segment includes Pharmacy Benefit Services and Specialty and Care Services, offering pharmacy benefit management, drug claim adjudication, retail pharmacy network administration, benefit design consultation, drug utilization review, drug formulary management, pharmacy benefits, home delivery pharmacy, specialty pharmacy, specialty pharmaceutical distribution, and clinical programs for whole-person health outcomes. The Cigna Healthcare segment comprises U.S. Healthcare and International Health, delivering comprehensive medical and coordinated solutions such as employer medical plans, individual and family plans, behavioral health, consumer health engagement, dental, pharmacy management, stop-loss insurance, global health care, and local health care solutions, as well as health care benefits for mobile individuals and employees of multinational organizations. The company offers other operations, including corporate-owned life insurance, reinsurance, and certain run-off and non-strategic businesses. The company distributes its products and services through brokers and consultants; directly to employers, unions and other groups, or individuals; and private and public exchanges. The company was formerly known as Cigna Corporation and changed its name to The Cigna Group in February 2023. The company was founded in 1792 and is headquartered in Bloomfield, Connecticut.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Brian Case Evanko C.F.A. | President, CEO & Director | Age 48 | Compensation: $3.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 65K people. Revenue per employee of $4.2M ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers, improving at 28%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["The Cigna Group is a large-cap healthcare business with a $77.6B market cap on $274.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +15% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 6.6\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 6.5% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.09964280029416432},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $65.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 47% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 8/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","43 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Financial quality scores above most Healthcare peers","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Cigna projects at least $30.60 2026 adjusted EPS while targeting $3B gross savings by 2030 (NYSE:CI)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4667558-cigna-projects-at-least-30_60-2026-adjusted-eps-while-targeting-3b-gross-savings-by-2030","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793918855.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Cigna Group (CI) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/cigna-group-ci-q3-2026-201754000.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793910761.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Cigna Group (CI) Raises 2026 Outlook After Strong Quarter And $3 Billion Reset","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/cigna-group-ci-raises-2026-191205466.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793905925.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.949,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Compared to Estimates, Cigna (CI) Q3 Earnings: A Look at Key Metrics","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3024171/compared-to-estimates-cigna-ci-q3-earnings-a-look-at-key-metrics?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cnfm-3024171","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793885402.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Cigna Delivers Strong Q3, Accelerate To One Program Targets $3B Savings By 2030","source":"benzinga.com","link":"https://www.benzinga.com/analyst-stock-ratings/price-target/26/11/62996021/cigna-delivers-strong-q3-accelerate-to-one-program-targets-3b-savings-by-2030","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793985064.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":1,"scope":"co